        "original_id": "ee0e7264-74a1-5020-922e-2e7fd57299ef",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Vincenzo Bellini, Mikhail Glinka\n- Works: I puritani, Kamarinskaya\n- Topics: opera, Russian classical music, Russian folk dance\n\nFacts:\n- Vincenzo Bellini was born on 3 November 1801 and died on 23 September 1835.\n- Vincenzo Bellini was an Italian opera composer known for his long-flowing melodic lines and was called \"the Swan of Catania.\"\n- Mikhail Glinka was born on 1 June 1804 (20 May O.S.) and died on 15 February 1857 (3 February O.S.).\n- Mikhail Glinka was the first Russian composer to gain wide recognition within Russia and is often regarded as the fountainhead of Russian classical music.\n- I puritani is an opera by Vincenzo Bellini.\n- Kamarinskaya is a Russian traditional folk dance and is also the name of a composition by Mikhail Glinka.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
